course: dictionary
lesson: 9009
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means. Skimmer is a good example: it can be a kitchen spoon, a bird, or a device on a cash machine.
explain: «A skimmer is a fake device fitted to a cash machine to steal card details; if a machine looks odd, use another and tell the bank.» The clues are fake, steal and card details. Nobody fits a spoon to a cash machine to steal from people, so a skimmer here is a hidden device, not a kitchen tool.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If you swap in "a flat spoon", the sentence stops making sense. That tells you that you have picked the wrong meaning.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multi-meaning word. The sentence tells you which meaning is used.
fact: «Skimmer» can mean a flat spoon with holes, used to lift foam off soup or jam.
fact: A skimmer is also a seabird that flies low and skims fish from the water's surface with its long lower beak.
fact: In crime, a skimmer is a hidden device that criminals fit to cash machines to steal card details.
fact: To stay safe at a cash machine, cover your PIN with your other hand and tell an adult if anything looks odd.
exercise: «A skimmer is a fake device fitted to a cash machine to steal card details.» What is a skimmer in this sentence? | A flat spoon for lifting foam off soup | *A hidden device criminals use to steal card details | A seabird that catches fish
exercise: Mum says, «Lift the foam off the jam with the skimmer.» What is the skimmer here? | A cash machine | A seabird that flies low over the sea | A machine that cleans oil from water | *A flat spoon with holes
exercise: A skimmer flies low over the sea and skims fish from the water with its long lower beak. What is it? | A cash machine | A kitchen spoon | A reader who reads quickly | *A seabird
test: Which meaning of skimmer fits a stone that skips over water? | A seabird that eats fish | A device that cleans oil from a pool | A flat spoon with holes | *Something that skims, such as a stone that skips over water
test: «The oil spill was cleaned up by a skimmer that floated on the water.» What does skimmer mean here? | *A device that removes oil from the surface of water | A stone that skips | A flat spoon with holes | A bird that eats fish
exam: «Ella saw a skimmer fitted to a cash machine and told the bank.» What is the best meaning here? | A reader who reads quickly | A seabird with a long beak | A flat spoon with holes | *A hidden device used by criminals to steal card details
